{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "Tune26 / S4.1 / D2.4.1 / D3.3.3v3: ord(any) returns a checked int|null Item, and a plain int declaration calls its sole, cold lambda_type_check only off the int arm; the int path must not box and dynamically traverse the already closed result. Re-pinned 2026-09-27 (S11.4.3, LR12-36): `value: any` may hold an error, which is now ord's value instead of a return from decode before the call. The operand's error tag (27) is tested ahead of fn_ord and joined with its result, the declaration branches on that join's int tag straight into the cold check, and decode keeps only its normal and stack-overflow returns.",
  "checks": [
    {
      "in_func": "_decode_#",
      "expect_seq": [
        {
          "pattern": "eq\t{{r}}, {{r}}, 27"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "call\tfn_ord_p, fn_ord"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "\tbne\t"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "call\tlambda_type_check_p, lambda_type_check"
        }
      ],
      "count": {
        "call\tfn_ord_p, fn_ord": 1,
        "call\tlambda_type_check_p, lambda_type_check": 1,
        "\tret\t": 2
      }
    }
  ]
}
